# ============================================================================
#  Lantern Row — Night Two
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Augie Prell
=== augie_start
? {augie.camera_returned} -> augie_after
? {has:camera} -> augie_return
? {augie.met} -> augie_again
~ remember augie met
Augie: Evening. Morning. Whatever this is. You're the Deadhouse woman — the one with the wagon.
Ines: Depends who's asking.
Augie: Augie Prell. Portraits, weddings, and the occasional husband who isn't where he said he'd be.
* [wry] A photographer who works in the dark. -> augie_dark
* [blunt] I'm asking about Tomas Reyes. -> augie_tomas
* [cold] I don't buy pictures. -> augie_cold

=== augie_dark
Augie: Best light there is. Nobody poses.
-> augie_offer

=== augie_cold
~ remember augie ines_cold
Augie: Nobody buys pictures. They buy the negatives. Afterwards.
-> augie_offer

=== augie_tomas
Augie: Reyes. The one they carried out to you in a tablecloth.
> He says it too fast. He's been waiting for someone to ask.
-> augie_offer

=== augie_offer
Augie: I might have something for you. A picture. The Velour's side door, two nights back, ten past two in the morning. You'd want to see who's holding the door.
Ines: And what does it cost me?
Augie: My camera. Hobb took it. Collecting on a debt, he said — he'll sell it back when I can afford my own hands.
Augie: He keeps the top floor of the Garnet Arms. Number fourteen, this end of the block. His boys keep the stairs.
* [warm] I'll get it back for you. -> augie_deal_warm
* [blunt] Why not go yourself? -> augie_why
* [wry] You want me to walk into a debt collector's house. For a photograph. -> augie_why

=== augie_why
Augie: Because I've been up those stairs, and I came down with less than I took up. Look at me. Do I look like a man who goes back?
Augie: You've got a look. Like you've already seen the worst thing that happens to people, and then you did the paperwork.
-> augie_deal

=== augie_deal_warm
~ remember augie ines_kind
Augie: ...Yeah. All right. Thank you. Nobody says that on the Row unless they want something.
-> augie_deal

=== augie_deal
~ set quest.camera
Augie: It's a press camera, brown leather case. There are prints tucked in the lid. Please — don't look at the prints.
-> END

=== augie_again
Augie: Number fourteen. Top floor. Brown leather case.
? {stance:cold>=2} -> augie_again_cold
-> END

=== augie_again_cold
Augie: You don't have to like me, Deadhouse. Just bring it back.
-> END

=== augie_return
Augie: Is that — you got it. You actually got it.
? {looked_at_prints} -> augie_return_looked
-> augie_return_clean

=== augie_return_looked
> He opens the lid. Thumbs the prints. His face goes very still.
Augie: These are out of order.
* [blunt] I looked. -> augie_honest
* [cold] Hobb's men, probably. -> augie_lie
* [warm] I wanted to know what I was carrying. -> augie_honest_warm

=== augie_honest
~ remember augie ines_honest
Augie: ...Right. Then you know why Hobb wanted it. And why I want it more.
-> augie_photo

=== augie_honest_warm
~ remember augie ines_honest
Augie: Can't say I wouldn't have. Just — that man pays my rent, in a manner of speaking. Forget his face. He'd want you to.
-> augie_photo

=== augie_lie
~ remember augie ines_lied
Augie: Sure. Hobb's men.
> He doesn't believe you. He's polite enough not to say so, and that's worse.
-> augie_photo

=== augie_return_clean
~ remember augie trusts_ines
Augie: And the prints are still in order. God bless you, Deadhouse. I mean it.
-> augie_photo

=== augie_photo
~ take camera
~ give photo
~ remember augie camera_returned
~ set quest.camera_done
Augie: Here. Ten past two, the Velour's side door. That's Reyes coming out. Looks sick, doesn't he? Or drunk.
Augie: And that's Lionel Gaunt holding the door for him. Vivienne Sabler's floor manager. Carnation and all.
Augie: Whatever happened to Reyes, it started inside that club. I'd bet my hands on it.
~ call camera_returned
-> END

=== augie_after
? {augie.ines_lied} -> augie_after_cool
Augie: If you ever need a picture taken, Deadhouse — any picture — you come to me first.
-> END

=== augie_after_cool
Augie: Evening.
> Friendly. Careful. Both at once.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Vivienne Sabler
=== viv_start
? {viv.met} -> viv_again
~ remember viv met
> A woman in black silk under the canopy, smoking as if she'd paid for the rain.
Vivienne (amused): The Deadhouse sends its wagon to my door twice in one week. People will talk.
Ines: People were already talking.
Vivienne (neutral): Vivienne Sabler. I own the noise coming through these walls. And you're the woman who takes my customers away when they stop breathing.
* [wry] Only the ones who don't tip. -> viv_wry
* [blunt] Tomas Reyes walked out of your club and ended up on my table. -> viv_blunt
* [cold] I'm not here to make friends. -> viv_cold
* [warm] You look like you came out for the air. -> viv_warm

=== viv_wry
~ remember viv liked_joke
Vivienne (amused): Then you'd have a very crowded table.
-> viv_mid

=== viv_blunt
~ remember viv pressed_early
Vivienne (cold): Half this city walks out of my club and ends up somewhere worse. I sell them the evening. I don't sell them the morning.
-> viv_mid

=== viv_cold
Vivienne (neutral): Good. Friends ask for credit.
-> viv_mid

=== viv_warm
~ remember viv saw_through
Vivienne (warm): ...I did. Don't tell anyone. In there they think I don't need anything at all.
-> viv_mid

=== viv_mid
Vivienne (neutral): Next you'll ask me about Hobb. Everyone with that look on their face asks about Hobb.
* [blunt] What do you know about him? -> viv_hobb
* {augie.met} [wry] Augie Prell sends his regards. -> viv_augie
* [cold] I'll ask what I like. -> viv_hobb_cold

=== viv_augie
Vivienne (amused): Augie sends his regards to everyone. Usually in an envelope, with a price on it.
-> viv_hobb

=== viv_hobb_cold
Vivienne (amused): And I'll answer what I like. It's a fair arrangement.
-> viv_hobb

=== viv_hobb
Vivienne (neutral): Hobb collects. For a man who never comes to the Row himself. He keeps boys on the stairs of Fourteen, and a gun in his coat he loves more than his mother.
? {viv.saw_through | viv.liked_joke} -> viv_tip
Vivienne (cold): That's all you get for free.
-> viv_close

=== viv_tip
~ remember viv gave_tip
~ set tip.fire_escape
Vivienne (warm): His boys watch the stairs. Nobody watches the fire escape. Hobb thinks the alley is beneath him.
-> viv_close

=== viv_close
Vivienne (amused): Come inside some night when you're not carrying anyone. Bruno lets in anything that isn't wearing a uniform.
* [warm] Maybe I will. -> viv_flirt
* [wry] I'll ask the dead if they can spare me. -> viv_flirt_wry
* [cold] I'm always carrying someone. -> viv_end_cold

=== viv_flirt
~ remember viv interested
Vivienne (warm): Maybe you will. I'll have them keep the lights low. You look like a woman who's tired of being seen by daylight.
-> END

=== viv_flirt_wry
~ remember viv interested
Vivienne (amused): The dead can always spare you. It's the living who keep count.
-> END

=== viv_end_cold
Vivienne (neutral): Then put them down sometime. They're heavier than they look.
-> END

=== viv_again
? {has:photo} -> viv_photo
? {viv.shown_photo} -> viv_after_show
Vivienne (amused): Still out here? The rain suits you. The coat doesn't.
-> END

=== viv_photo
> You could show her the photograph. Her floor manager, holding the door for a man who'd be dead by morning.
* [blunt] Show her. -> viv_show
* [cold] Keep it to yourself. For now. -> viv_hold

=== viv_show
~ remember viv shown_photo
~ set quest.viv_shown
Vivienne (cold): Lionel. Of course it's Lionel.
Vivienne (neutral): Put that away before anyone inside sees it. Not here. Not with the whole block watching. Ask me again when the Row has gone to bed.
> [The Velour, Lionel Gaunt and Vivienne's answer are beyond Prototype 1. This thread continues in the vertical slice.]
-> END

=== viv_hold
~ remember viv photo_withheld
Vivienne (amused): You've got a secret. It shows. It suits you better than the coat.
-> END

=== viv_after_show
Vivienne (neutral): Not tonight, Ines. I said not tonight.
> She knows your name. You never gave it to her.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Bruno
=== bruno_start
? {viv.interested} -> bruno_viv
Bruno: Deliveries round back. And round back is closed.
* [wry] I'm not delivering. I'm collecting. -> bruno_wry
* [blunt] I need to get inside. -> bruno_no
* [cold] Never mind. -> END

=== bruno_wry
Bruno: Then you're definitely round back.
-> END

=== bruno_no
Bruno: Not in that coat. Not tonight. Nothing personal. I don't do personal.
-> END

=== bruno_viv
Bruno: She said you might come back. She also said "not tonight." She says a lot of things.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Sully
=== sully_start
? {sully.lit} -> sully_after
Sully: Lady. Lady. Got a light? This rain's got into every match in Corvane.
-> sully_ask

=== sully_ask
* {has:matches} [warm] Here. -> sully_light
* [wry] Do I know you? -> sully_know
* [cold] Keep walking. -> sully_no

=== sully_know
Sully: Everybody knows Sully. Sully knows everybody. That's the whole economy, lady.
-> sully_ask

=== sully_light
~ remember sully lit
> You strike a match inside your coat. He leans into it like a confession.
Sully: Bless you. Bless you. Listen — you're going into Fourteen, aren't you? You've got the face for it.
Sully: The Dunne brothers drink in the hall downstairs. The skinny one with the knife sits on the second landing, jumpy as a cat — scared of the dark, if you ask me. And Hobb never comes down. Never.
~ set tip.tenement
-> END

=== sully_no
Sully: Everybody's a critic.
-> END

=== sully_after
Sully: Warmest I've been all week. You need anything on the Row, you ask for Sully.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- places
=== hotel_door
> ROOMS BY THE HOUR — CASH — NO QUESTIONS. The night clerk looks up, looks at your coat, and goes back to his newspaper.
Clerk: We're full. We're always full for the Deadhouse.
-> END

=== phone
> The receiver is warm. Somebody was just here. The coin slot's been jammed with a matchstick.
? {quest.camera} -> phone_think
-> END

=== phone_think
> You could call the Deadhouse and tell Dr. Abernathy where you are. He'd tell you to come back. You hang up.
-> END

=== marquee_door
> Planks nailed over the staff door, newer than the rest of the boarding. Through the gaps, cold light flickers: twenty-four times a second. Someone is running a projector inside a cinema that closed in 1931.
? {remnant:maud} -> END
> The wood is soft with rain. Someone strong enough could take it down. You aren't. Not alone.
-> END

=== wagon
> The wagon ticks as it cools. CITY MORGUE, the door says, in letters someone repaints every spring.
* [Prototype] Use the test kit: grant Maud Kessel's Lesson (Break) -> wagon_kit
* Leave it. -> END

=== wagon_kit
? {remnant:maud} -> wagon_kit_done
~ call grant_maud
> PROTOTYPE NOTE: in the full game Maud is acquired in the Sumps (Night Two, the cellar fight ring). Here she is granted so the boarded door can be tested.
-> END

=== wagon_kit_done
> Maud is already with you. She's been cracking her knuckles for an hour.
-> END
